<div class="case-content">
  <section class="case-block split">
    <div>
      <div class="section-label">BUSINESS QUESTION</div>
      <h2>Revenue is growing. Why is margin still under pressure?</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="case-copy">
      <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A synthetic offshore services company is running above its revenue budget during 2026, but EBITDA margin is not expanding at the same pace.</p>
      <p>The finance team needs to update the remaining-month forecast, understand the main cost drivers and provide leadership with a clear view of expected full-year performance.</p>
      <p><strong>Objective:</strong> connect operational performance to the P&L and highlight the actions required to protect profitability.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-block">
    <div class="section-label">EXECUTIVE VIEW</div>
    <h2>2026 rolling forecast</h2>
    <div class="kpis">
      <div class="kpi"><span>Forecast Revenue</span><strong>$51.7M</strong><em>+7.1% vs Budget</em></div>
      <div class="kpi"><span>Forecast EBITDA</span><strong>$9.6M</strong><em>18.6% margin</em></div>
      <div class="kpi"><span>Revenue Upside</span><strong>$3.4M</strong><em>FY variance</em></div>
      <div class="kpi"><span>Forecast CAPEX</span><strong>$5.6M</strong><em>~on budget</em></div>
    </div>
    <table class="case-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Metric ($mm)</th><th>Budget</th><th>Forecast</th><th>Variance</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Revenue</td><td>48.3</td><td>51.7</td><td class="positive">+3.4</td></tr>
        <tr><td>COGS</td><td>26.5</td><td>28.9</td><td class="negative">+2.4</td></tr>
        <tr><td>OPEX</td><td>12.4</td><td>13.2</td><td class="negative">+0.8</td></tr>
        <tr><td>EBITDA</td><td>9.3</td><td>9.6</td><td class="positive">+0.3</td></tr>
        <tr><td>CAPEX</td><td>5.6</td><td>5.6</td><td>-</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="case-block">
    <div class="section-label">VARIANCE BRIDGE</div>
    <h2>Growth is being absorbed by cost pressure.</h2>
    <div class="waterfall">
      <div class="wf"><b>$9.3M</b><i style="height:72%"></i><small>Budget<br>EBITDA</small></div>
      <div class="wf"><b class="positive">+$3.4M</b><i style="height:44%"></i><small>Revenue<br>Upside</small></div>
      <div class="wf"><b class="negative">-$2.4M</b><i style="height:35%"></i><small>COGS<br>Pressure</small></div>
      <div class="wf"><b class="negative">-$0.8M</b><i style="height:18%"></i><small>OPEX<br>Run-rate</small></div>
      <div class="wf"><b>$9.6M</b><i style="height:76%"></i><small>Forecast<br>EBITDA</small></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-block">
    <div class="section-label">MANAGEMENT INTERPRETATION</div>
    <h2>What I would communicate to leadership.</h2>
    <div class="management-grid">
      <div><strong>1. What changed?</strong><p>Revenue and commercial performance are above plan, creating a meaningful top-line upside.</p></div>
      <div><strong>2. What is the risk?</strong><p>Higher supplier, logistics and mobilization costs are consuming most of the revenue benefit.</p></div>
      <div><strong>3. What should happen next?</strong><p>Reforecast remaining-month COGS and OPEX, review high-impact cost drivers weekly and preserve disciplined CAPEX timing.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-block split">
